   "source": [
    "# Select Heavy Truck records\n",
    "heavy_truck = df1[df1[\"Vehicle_Type\"] == \"Heavy Truck\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a boxplot of CO2 emissions \n",
    "plt.figure(figsize = (8,5))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.boxplot(heavy_truck[\"Carbon_Emission_kgCO2e\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add labels and title\n",
    "plt.title(\"CO2 Emissions for Heavy Trucks\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Carbon Emissions (kgCO2e)\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Heavy Trucks\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display the boxplot\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62d0fee6-958e-47e8-9781-37bbdd0cd581",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Conclusion:\n",
    "The boxplot highloghts the distribution of CO2 emissions for Heavy Truck deliveries. There are five observations above the upper whisker which may be considered as outliers in the dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6e883934-51de-4a2d-98b7-db28861812c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Question 3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "6bec456e-1f5c-459f-91d6-688420c13346",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Upper threshold: 1137.7332499999998\n",
      "Outlier emissions:\n",
      "1602    1280.173\n",
      "1773    1168.420\n",
      "5548    1172.789\n",
      "7875    1200.512\n",
      "8265    1209.977\n",
      "Name: Carbon_Emission_kgCO2e, dtype: float64\n",
      "Number of records: 11995\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Select Heavy Truck records\n",
    "heavy_truck = df1[df1[\"Vehicle_Type\"] == \"Heavy Truck\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate quartiles and IQR\n",
    "Q1 = heavy_truck[\"Carbon_Emission_kgCO2e\"].quantile(0.25)\n",
    "Q3 = heavy_truck[\"Carbon_Emission_kgCO2e\"].quantile(0.75)\n",
    "\n",
    "IQR = Q3 - Q1\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate the upper whisker threshold\n",
    "upper_whisker = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Upper threshold:\", upper_whisker)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Identify emissions above the upper threshold\n",
    "outliers = heavy_truck[\n",
    "    heavy_truck[\"Carbon_Emission_kgCO2e\"] > upper_whisker]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Outlier emissions:\")\n",
    "print(outliers[\"Carbon_Emission_kgCO2e\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove these records from the original dataset\n",
    "df_filtered = df1.drop(outliers.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check the number of remaining records\n",
    "print(\"Number of records:\", df_filtered.shape[0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c9ed3e48-9261-441a-b639-d2ea91f6f191",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Conclusion\n",
    "Using IQR method, five Heavy Truck records were identified as outliers because their CO2 emissions were higher the upper threshold. After these outliers were removed, 11,995 records remained in the dataset. "
   ]
  },
